WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.293
Every township produces sewage and food waste.

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:08.516
The sewage already flows to a treatment plant. With proper segregation, food waste can also become a useful feedstock.

00:00:08.516 --> 00:00:13.417
Today, the STP uses electricity and generates sludge that must be managed.

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:17.502
What if part of that waste could help recover value?

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:23.176
A site-designed biodigester can process suitable STP sludge, with prepared food waste added where feasible.

00:00:23.176 --> 00:00:26.958
Microorganisms break down the organic material in a sealed tank.

00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:31.046
This process produces biogas containing methane. We capture and clean the gas,

00:00:31.046 --> 00:00:35.474
then use it to generate electricity for the STP or other common services.

00:00:35.474 --> 00:00:39.025
Digestion also leaves digestate. After dewatering, treatment and testing,

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:42.971
suitable material can be processed into fertilizer or soil conditioner.

00:00:42.971 --> 00:00:47.301
For an existing township, we assess the STP, waste supply and available space.

00:00:47.301 --> 00:00:50.964
Then we design the biodigester and connections to fit the site.

00:00:50.964 --> 00:00:56.057
For a new development, recovery can be considered while the STP and utilities are being designed.

00:00:56.057 --> 00:00:59.558
That helps coordinate space, connections and system capacity from the start.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:03.343
You already own an STP. Don’t consider it just a cost.

00:01:03.343 --> 00:01:07.473
Let us help turn it into a money-making machine while helping nature.
